=================================ARIMA-GARCH Time Series Forecasting & Volatility Modeling============================================
## 🇬🇧 English
This project demonstrates a complete time series forecasting workflow using a hybrid **ARIMA-GARCH** approach.

The objective is to model both::
Expected Return (Mean Process) using ARIMA
Volatility / Risk (Variance Process) using GARCH

The project simulates financial price data, transforms it into stationary log returns, analyzes autocorrelation patterns, forecasts future returns, and estimates conditional volatility.

---
Technologies & Libraries::
Python
NumPy
Pandas
Matplotlib
Statsmodels
ARCH

---
Project Workflow::
Financial Price Simulation:
A synthetic financial price series is generated using a Random Walk process.
Stationarity Analysis:
Since ARIMA models require stationary data, prices are transformed into logarithmic returns and evaluated using the Augmented Dickey-Fuller (ADF) test.
ACF & PACF Analysis:
Autocorrelation (ACF) and Partial Autocorrelation (PACF) plots are used to investigate the dependency structure of the series and guide ARIMA parameter selection.
ARIMA Modeling:
An ARIMA(1,0,1) model is fitted to capture the mean behavior of returns.
GARCH Modeling:
Residuals from the ARIMA model are used to fit a GARCH(1,1) model in order to estimate time-varying volatility and risk.
Forecasting:
The model generates:
Next-period expected return
Next-period expected volatility

---
